      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay so you're saying there are legit issues like cybersecurity and counting discrepancies. if those things are actually possible, then isn't it dangerous to just assume everything is fine? it feels like the \"consensus\" is basically just a way to shut down anyone who thinks things are broken. if you had to pick, do you think the current safeguards are actually enough to prevent a major manipulation, or are they just a band-aid on a fundamentally broken system?",
